# GitNexus (contributor)

If you are operating a running instance, ignore this rule. Follow
`thytrader-agent-operations` instead. Do not bootstrap GitNexus, edit `src/`,
or update documentation from `ops/`.

GitNexus is required for contributor work in this repository. If it is not
available — no MCP tools, no `.gitnexus/run.cjs`, `Cannot find module`, empty
or unregistered index, or `gitnexus` not on PATH — bootstrap from the
repository root **before editing**. Do not skip impact analysis or
`detect_changes` because the graph was absent at session start.

Once `.gitnexus/run.cjs` exists:

```bash
node .gitnexus/run.cjs analyze --embeddings --pdg --index-only
```

If that file is missing, bootstrap (then use `node .gitnexus/run.cjs` for
impact / detect-changes). Prefer `bunx` on npm 11, where `npx gitnexus` can
crash (`node.target is null`; GitNexus #1939):

```bash
bunx gitnexus@latest analyze --embeddings --pdg --index-only
```

`npx gitnexus analyze` and `pnpm dlx gitnexus@latest analyze` are equivalents.
See `.claude/skills/gitnexus-cli/SKILL.md` and root `AGENTS.md` § Use GitNexus
first. Do not copy this duty into `ops/` instruction files.
